WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.600
Today marks

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.268
one year into Russia's full scale

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.737
invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.672
There's no real end in sight right now

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.874
after 12 months of intense fighting.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.843
The Ukrainian president

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.344
Zelensky is declaring

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.980
that the war will end in 2023.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.181
I sat down with Defense

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.182
Secretary Lloyd Austin

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:16.850
outside of his office

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.685
of the Pentagon yesterday for his view

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.719
on where the war stands,

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.055
how he thinks it could end

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.858
When you look at this

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.393
and you're making your assessment,

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.729
do you think this ends with negotiations

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.398
or does it end on the battlefield?

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.565
Most likely

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.266
it will end

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.870
with some sort of negotiation.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.572
And what the Ukrainians are interested in

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.641
is getting there,

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.409
getting the Russians

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.310
out of their sovereign territory.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.678
And I think that's probably going

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.080
to be either going in

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.381
a point where,

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:48.681
you know,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.682
I'll let the Ukrainians

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.517
speak for themselves.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:51.918
Also,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.118
and I

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.786
also discussed

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.253
the threats

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:53.820
that are posed

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.655
by China and US's concerns

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.323
about Beijing considering

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.325
potentially providing Russia with lethal

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.493
military assistance.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.761
Here's what he said.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:03.930
We heard recently

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.432
the US revealing some intelligence.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.032
They do believe

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.001
China is preparing to provide

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.702
potentially lethal assistance

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.805
to Russia to help them in Ukraine.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.440
Tell us what you're seeing

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.511
We've not seen any China provide

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.780
any material assistance to Ukraine

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.282
or to Russia at this point.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.216
China hasn't

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.985
taken it off the table for sure.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.621
I've engaged my counterpart early on

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.924
and told him that

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.159
this this would be a very bad mistake

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.694
if if China were to do this

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.162
would further complicate things.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.630
And you think they're preparing

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.398
to do that?

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:41.167
I don't I can't speak for the Chinese.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.435
I mean, they have

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.971
tremendous capabilities and so,

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.207
again, if they were to do that,

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.575
it would be ill advised

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.576
when it comes to that.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.076
If they

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.511
if they do take that step

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.913
and China does move to provide

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.449
lethal assistance to Russia for this.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.917
What are the consequences going to

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:58.885
look like for China?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.421
Well, you

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.589
know, of course,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.091
there's a reputational risk in

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.426
and of course,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.728
I'm sure China would love to enjoy

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.163
a good relationship

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.731
with all the countries in Europe.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.600
And and and again,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.968
if you just look at the numbers

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.370
of countries around the world

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.406
that that really think that

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:24.010
what Russia has done is is horrible.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.412
I mean, adding to that,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.481
I think China would be a very,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.783
very ill-Advised step for China to take.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.418
Would it significantly help

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.220
Russia, though, if they did that?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:34.554
How much

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:35.221
how much of a blow

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.789
would that be for the Ukrainians

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.590
if Russia starts

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.159
getting that kind of assistance

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.360
from China?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.261
Well, you know, again,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.095
I don't want to

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.731
get into hypotheticals, but it's clear

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.833
that China has a lot of capability

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.401
in terms of munitions and weapons.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.104
And if they they provide the

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:52.739
sort of,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.508
you know, substantial support to Russia,

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.144
it prolongs the conflict with China.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.680
Recently, the tensions have gotten worse

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.848
between the United States and China,

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:02.815
especially after the US

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.617
shut down that surveillance balloon.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.451
You tried to call

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.619
your Chinese counterpart

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.088
and they didn't answer.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:09.689
Yeah.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.724
So on the day that that happened,

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.326
my office reached out his office

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.794
to schedule a call

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.963
and they did not schedule the call.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:18.865
That's

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.601
not really

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.503
you've heard me say a number of times.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.837
Kate, one that I think

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.606
it's really, really important to

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.576
to make sure that we maintain lines

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.810
of communication open.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.246
And I think leaders

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.315
need to be able to talk to each other to

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.885
avoid misperceptions and, and

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.386
and manage crises.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.989
And so this is really important.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.159
And so we hope that minister way

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.994
well we'll have a change of heart

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.163
and in schedule that call

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.332
When was the last time you talked to him?

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.601
The last time that I talked to him

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.569
was a couple of months ago, so.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.403
Well,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.671
I mean, how concerning is that

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.840
that the secretary of defense in the US

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.909
can't get your counterpart

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:03.843
in China on the phone.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:05.979
Again, I think there's

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:06.946
risk involved with that.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.281
I think it's important

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:08.815
to be

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:09.782
It's not like

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.884
we don't have any lines of communication

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:12.151
open.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.286
You just saw

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.153
Secretary Blinken

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.322
talk to his counterpart in in Munich.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.992
And so their diplomatic lines

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.026
of communication open.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.195
But but I think for the military, it's

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.297
really, really important that we maintain

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.932
open lines of communication.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:26.432
And right now,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.900
there's not really one between the U.S.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.535
military and the Chinese military.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.169
That's that's right.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.170
But but it doesn't

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.472
mean that there won't be one.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.740
So I think,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.707
you know, we'll continue

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.342
to make sure that

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.744
we stress the importance of this.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.212
And hopefully, Minister,

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.447
we will schedule that call.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.715
He knows where to find him.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.117
He knows where to find you

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.318
when it comes to

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.452
shooting down the balloon.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.320
What that looks like,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:47.887
there were questions

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.689
about whether President Xi knew

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.257
about exactly

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.125
where the balloon was going,

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:52.892
what it was doing.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.560
Is there a disconnect, in your sense,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.529
between the Chinese president and

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.430
his own military

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.166
That could be.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.034
I think

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:01.634
the Chinese

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.935
will have to answer that question.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.038
But but

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.641
it could very well

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.409
be that

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:11.177
that he was not informed of

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:11.978
what was going on.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.845
When it comes to the US

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.814
response on these spy balloons.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:15.581
We saw several

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.983
shut down within a matter of days.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.651
We haven't seen any that we know of

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.919
that have been shut down

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:20.820
in the last several days.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.355
Is that because we're not seeing any?

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.157
Or the United States is deciding

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.224
and changing the threshold

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.559
of what it's shooting down

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.195
and when there have been no

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:30.797
threats reported?

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:31.731
No, no,

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:32.498
no balloons

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.434
that have been reported to me

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.402
that we need to be concerned about.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.272
But we'll evaluate each

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:42.141
each case on its own merits.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.545
Caitlin, you know, we'll assess the

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:48.948
the issue.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:49.716
If it's a threat,

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:50.983
you know, we'll deal with it.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.785
In the case of these three balloons

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:55.021
that we engaged

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.256
before, they were all operating in

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.459
in airspace

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.094
that would present a hazard

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:03.763
to civilian air traffic.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:07.500
And they had travel routes that

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.068
passed by our

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.770
are some of our sensitive sites.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.371
And whether or not

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.139
they had the ability to collect,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.340
you know, we don't know.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.043
But an exercise

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.945
using an abundance of caution,

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:21.114
we we decided to take them back.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.315
Is that a pretty jarring

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.883
blind spot, though, that the US had

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:24.450
when it came

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.018
to what we learned about the balloons

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.787
that actually happened

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:28.421
during the Trump

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.323
administration, that those top officials,

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:30.690
you know,

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.657
your predecessor said

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.526
they didn't know about?

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.160
Well, we've

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.595
we've learned a lot

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.362
over the years

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.997
as we've continued to focus

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.465
on this problem set.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.167
And and certainly,

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:43.636
you know, we use that

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:45.405
knowledge and analyzing

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.073
what not only what happened in the past,

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.841
but what's happening now

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.476
and what could happen in the future.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.111
And Taiwan is obviously a major

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.346
part of this.

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:54.480
There are reports that the U.S.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.982
is preparing to send more U.S.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.583
military forces to Taiwan.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.885
Is that accurate?

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.521
I won't comment on troop deployments

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.223
or operations or our training.

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:05.291
What I will tell

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:05.825
you, Caitlin,

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.893
is we remain committed

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:09.295
to supporting Taiwan

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:10.430
in accordance

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.798
with the Taiwan Relations Act.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.332
We're going to do everything

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:15.001
that we can to help them

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:17.036
acquire the means to defend themselves.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:17.770
The general,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:18.704
who's the head of Air

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.006
Mobility Command, recently

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:21.674
sent a memo out

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.443
saying that China in the US,

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.944
he believed, would be at war

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:25.678
two years from now.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:26.045
He said, quote,

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:28.548
My gut tells me we will fight in 20, 25.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.717
Is that true?

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:35.154
What you've heard me say in the past

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.022
and I'll say it again

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:38.324
today, is I don't see an imminent attack

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.560
by China on on Taiwan

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:43.563
And

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:46.766
what you have to

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.634
watch you know what we we

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.703
we can talk about what we see

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.773
and what we see is increased activity

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.509
by the Chinese and in the Taiwan Strait

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.410
that we've seen

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.779
a number of centerline line crossings

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.314
in the airspace.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:02.448
We've seen

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.516
increased activity

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.351
in the waters around Taiwan

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:09.522
as China continues to try to intimidate

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:11.224
Taiwan.

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:11.757
Given that,

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:12.558
why do you not think

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:13.459
an attack is imminent,

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:14.093
given you're seeing

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:15.962
that increased activity?

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.697
There are a number of reasons that,

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:18.164
you know,

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:19.532
that I won't go into here,

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.566
but I don't think it's

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.935
and she's best interest to

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:26.506
to attack Taiwan at this point in time.

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:29.375
And you have to judge them by by by

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.076
what you're seeing.

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:30.376
And again,

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.311
we are seeing increased activity.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.380
We got to make sure that we have

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:36.549
that we remain focused on this

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:38.851
and we have the ability to deter

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:40.953
China from from making a bad decision

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.622
and we will have that.

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.023
We have the capability now.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:45.324
We will continue to have the capability.

